From 5fe0910b77dcc02a452a76bcc78f05948d54daef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:15:16 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add xRX500 GSWIP-3.0 HAL core and Kconfig
 plumbing

Add the C-side core of the GSWIP-3.0 switch support:

 - gsw_flow_core.c: the per-instance device slot table, the
   gsw_get_swcore_ops() dispatch used by the other subsystems, and
   the four word/bitfield register accessors (gsw_r32/gsw_w32 and
   their raw forms) over the ioremapped switch window, exported in
   the GSWIP_INTERNAL symbol namespace.

 - gsw_init.c: the platform driver binding the two SoC switch
   instances ("intel,xrx500-gswip-3.0": GSW-L at 0x1c000000 and
   GSW-R at 0x1a000000). The probe allocates and populates the
   per-instance API device (structure layout ported from the vendor
   headers), registers it in the slot table, then runs the PCE
   microcode/core initialization added by the following patches;
   after the second instance has probed it triggers the one-time
   datapath registration.

 - Kconfig/Makefile: the INTEL_XRX500_NET suite gate (selecting the
   syscon/regmap/reset infrastructure the drivers need) and the
   INTEL_XRX500_GSWIP_API tristate that builds everything as one
   composite module, intel-xrx500-gswip. The suite is not yet wired
   into drivers/net/ethernet/Makefile; that happens in the final
   patch of the series, once every object referenced by the
   composite exists, so the tree builds at every step.

Both C files are derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release
(Linux 4.9.198) switch-api module - Copyright (c) 2012-2015 Lantiq
Deutschland GmbH, (c) 2016-2017 Intel Corporation; notices added to
the files - with the register I/O rewritten for the v6.18 ioremap
world and the ioctl/external-MDIO surface dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
